{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Like the citizen among you.</b> Just as a citizen accepts upon himself all the words of the Torah, so too a convert. From here they said: a convert who accepts upon himself all the words of the Torah except for one thing — they do not accept him. Rabbi Yosi son of Rabbi Yehuda says: even one small matter from the words of the scribes." "<b>For you were strangers in the land of Egypt.</b> Rashi explained: the blemish that is in you, do not mention to your fellow. And in Egypt, Israel served idolatry, as it is written at the end of Joshua: והסירו את אלהים אשר עבדו אבותיכם בעבר הנהר ובמצרים." "<b>And you shall love him as yourself.</b> Just as you want him to do for you, so you shall do for him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:42.076827982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}